(in-ns 'go.arbace.pysqlite3) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// Modules/_sqlite/: Copyright (C) 2004-2010 Gerhard Häring and the Python Software Foundation, under the PSF License"] [4 1 "// Agreement for Python 3.14 (LICENSE.md; the files' own zlib-style notices). The port to Go: Copyright (c) the Arbace"] [5 1 "// authors, under the same license."] [7 1 "// The module _sqlite3 (queue 215; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 215\"): CPython 3.14.10's Modules/_sqlite/"] [8 1 "// (module.c, connection.c, cursor.c, statement.c, row.c, blob.c, microprotocols.c, prepare_protocol.c, util.c, with"] [9 1 "// clinic's argument parsing) ported statement for statement over SQLite 3.50.4 itself, the amalgamation built by ci's"] [10 1 "// builder (arbace/clib/sqlite's node program) and called through arbace/clib, as _bz2, _lzma and _zstd are."] [11 1 "// Lib/sqlite3 is the tarball's Python over it."] [12 1 "//"] [13 1 "// Notes on the port:"] [14 1 "//   - SQLite calls C function pointers for the user-defined functions, aggregates, window functions, collations and"] [15 1 "//     the authorizer, progress and trace handlers: they are ci's natives here (callbacks.go), Go functions registered"] [16 1 "//     by name in ci.Natives before the library opens and handed to SQLite by tools/pyi/clib/sqlite/pysqlite.c's"] [17 1 "//     wrappers. A context pointer SQLite keeps (a callback_context, an aggregate's instance) is a handle of this"] [18 1 "//     package's table, an integer standing for the Go value."] [19 1 "//   - The library is built SQLITE_THREADSAFE=0 (sqlite3.threadsafety 0) and the GIL is held around every library call"] [20 1 "//     and callback (CPython releases it around the long ones): one C thread."] [21 1 "//   - \"PyErr_Occurred\" across a C call (a collation's exception surviving sqlite3_step, as CPython's thread state keeps"] [22 1 "//     it) is pending, set by the callbacks and taken where CPython tests it."] [23 1 "//   - The weak references the connection keeps to its cursors and blobs: the cursors' list is not kept (CPython only"] [24 1 "//     prunes it); the blobs are kept by the connection until it closes them."] [37 1 "// sqliteLib is the library's program, opened on the module's first use (its import), the natives registered first."] [50 1 "// cstring is a NUL-terminated copy of b in C memory (freed by the caller)."] [63 1 "// gostr is the C string at p (\"\" for NULL)."] [71 1 "// cbuf is a copy of b in C memory, at least one byte (freed by the caller)."] [86 1 "// pending is the error a callback left set (\"PyErr_Occurred\" after the C call returns)."] [95 1 "// chain is _PyErr_ChainExceptions1(exc) with err the error raised now: exc becomes its __context__."] [113 1 "// utf8 is PyUnicode_AsUTF8AndSize."] [119 1 "// fromUTF8 is PyUnicode_FromStringAndSize (strict)."] [136 1 "// checkBuffer is PyObject_CheckBuffer with PyObject_GetBuffer(PyBUF_SIMPLE): whether o exports a buffer, its bytes,"] [137 1 "// and the error of getting them (a memoryview not C-contiguous: BufferError)."] [152 1 "// PyLong_AsInt: an int or __index__, in a C int."] [158 1 "// asSsize is PyNumber_AsSsize_t(o, exc): exc on overflow (nil: OverflowError)."] [174 1 "// _pysqlite_long_as_int64"] [195 1 "// typeName is a type's tp_name as the C messages print it."] [198 1 "// badArgument is _PyArg_BadArgument."] [207 1 "// parseArgs is clinic's _PyArg_UnpackKeywords: names in order, the first posonly positional-only, those after maxpos"] [208 1 "// keyword-only, the first minargs required; the values by position (nil: absent)."] [281 1 "/* util.c */"] [283 1 "// Returns non-NULL if a new exception should be raised"] [330 1 "// set_error_from_code: nil when no exception need be raised."] [339 1 "// set_error_from_db checks the SQLite error code and gives the appropriate DB-API exception (nil: none)."] [346 2 "/* Create and set the exception. */"] [348 2 "// sqlite3_errmsg() always returns an UTF-8 encoded message"] [353 1 "// errOr is err, else a generic error (the C code's \"return NULL\" with an exception known set)."] [361 1 "// handles: the Go values SQLite holds as context pointers"] [369 23 "// aligned, never 0"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[132 52] [259 12] [259 25] [317 79] [324 69]]} (go/file "util.go" :imports [

    ;; Modules/_sqlite/: Copyright (C) 2004-2010 Gerhard Häring and the Python Software Foundation, under the PSF License
    ;; Agreement for Python 3.14 (LICENSE.md; the files' own zlib-style notices). The port to Go: Copyright (c) the Arbace
    ;; authors, under the same license.

    ;; The module _sqlite3 (queue 215; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "As built: 215"): CPython 3.14.10's Modules/_sqlite/
    ;; (module.c, connection.c, cursor.c, statement.c, row.c, blob.c, microprotocols.c, prepare_protocol.c, util.c, with
    ;; clinic's argument parsing) ported statement for statement over SQLite 3.50.4 itself, the amalgamation built by ci's
    ;; builder (arbace/clib/sqlite's node program) and called through arbace/clib, as _bz2, _lzma and _zstd are.
    ;; Lib/sqlite3 is the tarball's Python over it.
    ;;
    ;; Notes on the port:
    ;;   - SQLite calls C function pointers for the user-defined functions, aggregates, window functions, collations and
    ;;     the authorizer, progress and trace handlers: they are ci's natives here (callbacks.go), Go functions registered
    ;;     by name in ci.Natives before the library opens and handed to SQLite by tools/pyi/clib/sqlite/pysqlite.c's
    ;;     wrappers. A context pointer SQLite keeps (a callback_context, an aggregate's instance) is a handle of this
    ;;     package's table, an integer standing for the Go value.
    ;;   - The library is built SQLITE_THREADSAFE=0 (sqlite3.threadsafety 0) and the GIL is held around every library call
    ;;     and callback (CPython releases it around the long ones): one C thread.
    ;;   - "PyErr_Occurred" across a C call (a collation's exception surviving sqlite3_step, as CPython's thread state keeps
    ;;     it) is pending, set by the callbacks and taken where CPython tests it.
    ;;   - The weak references the connection keeps to its cursors and blobs: the cursors' list is not kept (CPython only
    ;;     prunes it); the blobs are kept by the connection until it closes them.


